description:
The topics covered will include the following:

     (1) Image acquisition and representation:

     * camera model and image formation;

     * sensing, sampling, quantization;

     * color representation and color spaces, human visual system;

     * image file formats.

     (2) Basic operations and intensity transformations:

     * image interpolation;

     * image thresholding;

     * contrast modification, histogram equalization and specification.

     (3) Spatial filtering:

     * image noise and artifacts;

     * linear systems and filters, convolution, correlation;

     * image smoothing, sharpening, template matching, other applications;

     * detecting edges and corners;

     * filtering color images.

     (4) Image segmentation:

     * region-based methods;

     * active contours;

     * mean shift.

     (5) Image restoration:


     * image degradations;

     * methods for image denoising, deblurring;

     * image quality evaluation metrics.

     (6) Frequency-domain processing:

     * Fourier transforms and their properties;

     * sampling theorem;

     * applications in image filtering.

     (7) Image compression:

     * coding, entropy;

     * JPEG;

     * multiscale image representations.

     (8) Morphological image processing.

     (9) Principal component analysis and applications in image processing, e.g., eigenfaces.

     (10) Deep neural networks for image processing:

     * neural network architectures;

     * loss functions and learning methods;

     * applications.
